.dirname(os.path.abspath(filepath)) or \".\"","intent":null,"tags":["Tool Misuse","llm-unconfirmed"],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":"f239fe898e7090985596902b5111ef3fb3133f3991fb13b1656c70b3bbdc433f","occurrences":[{"file":"src/auth.py","start_line":261,"end_line":null}]},{"id":"PE2","finding_id":"finding-b687f633d8d24a348352baf42c710c24","category":"Privilege Escalation","pattern":"Sudo/Root Execution","severity":"MEDIUM","confidence":0.8,"location":{"file":"src/auth.py","start_line":49,"end_line":null},"finding":"chmod 700","explanation":"Commands invoke sudo or root privileges. Verify this elevated access is necessary and justified.","remediation":"Avoid sudo/root unless strictly required. Prefer least-privilege patterns. If elevation is needed, document the justification and scope.","code_snippet":"        raise PermissionError(\n            f\"Refusing to persist credentials into {directory!r}: \"\n            \"directory is group- or world-writable. \"\n            \"Move the project to a private directory (chmod 700) first.\"\n        )\n\n","intent":null,"tags":["Privilege Escalation","llm-unconfirmed"],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":"6bed9d1d0486d5131ef68ab16b0104a5ea40d35575946e82db1dac741be2c028","occurrences":[{"file":"src/auth.py","start_line":49,"end_line":null}]},{"id":"PE2","finding_id":"finding-ab66281baff247c7a38e0d4be49f5c0b","category":"Privilege Escalation","pattern":"Sudo/Root Execution","severity":"MEDIUM","confidence":0.8,"location":{"file":"src/auth.py","start_line":140,"end_line":null},"finding":"chmod 600","explanation":"Commands invoke sudo or root privileges. Verify this elevated access is necessary and justified.","remediation":"Avoid sudo/root unless strictly required. Prefer least-privilege patterns. If elevation is needed, document the justification and scope.","code_snippet":"        if hasattr(os, \"geteuid\") and (st.st_mode & (stat.S_IRGRP | stat.S_IROTH)):\n            _logger.warning(\n                \"Ignoring credential file %s: permissions %o allow other users \"\n                \"to read it. Fix with: chmod 600 %s\",\n                filepath, st.st_mode & 0o777, filepath,\n            )\n            return","intent":null,"tags":["Privilege Escalation","llm-unconfirmed"],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":"fac387638fbcbc4ed94acb702b3cf68cbc839ee694afdddde6d97a39a3523b73","occurrences":[{"file":"src/auth.py","start_line":140,"end_line":null}]},{"id":"SDI-1","finding_id":"finding-b30cb514fff7402a81c908150c641838","category":null,"pattern":null,"severity":"MEDIUM","confidence":0.95,"location":{"file":"src/subtitle.py","start_line":321,"end_line":327},"finding":null,"explanation":"The module and class documentation present this file as a subtitle downloading and processing component, but the fallback path expands behavior into generating new subtitle-like text via audio transcription and fetching danmaku bullet comments as text references. Those are materially different capabilities from downloading existing subtitles and exceed the documented scope of this module.","remediation":"Update the module/class/skill documentation to explicitly disclose transcription and danmaku fallback behavior, or separate those features into distinct components so the subtitle module only downloads and converts official subtitle tracks.","code_snippet":null,"intent":null,"tags":["llm-unconfirmed"],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":null,"occurrences":[{"file":"src/subtitle.py","start_line":321,"end_line":327}]},{"id":"SQP-2","finding_id":"finding-85b45afeed194ca4b980c57cce5cc8e5","category":null,"pattern":null,"severity":"MEDIUM","confidence":0.89,"location":{"file":"src/subtitle.py","start_line":404,"end_line":454},"finding":null,"explanation":"When no subtitles are available, the code automatically downloads audio and generates a transcript on disk without explicit user opt-in at the point of fallback. This can create unexpected collection and persistence of derived content, which is a privacy and transparency problem, especially in agent environments where a user may have requested only subtitle retrieval.","remediation":"Require explicit user consent before invoking transcription fallback, and make it configurable with a clear flag such as allow_transcription_fallback=False by default. Also disclose that audio will be downloaded and derived transcript files written to disk, and provide options for ephemeral processing and automatic cleanup.","code_snippet":null,"intent":null,"tags":[],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":null,"occurrences":[{"file":"src/subtitle.py","start_line":404,"end_line":454}]},{"id":"SQP-3","finding_id":"finding-178b4c5ddf894057ae904cded648b968","category":null,"pattern":null,"severity":"MEDIUM","confidence":0.96,"location":{"file":"src/subtitle.py","start_line":419,"end_line":419},"finding":null,"explanation":"The transcription call forces `language=\"zh\"`, which imposes a specific language setting regardless of the user's preference or the video's actual language. This is a natural-language locale policy issue because the skill does not offer a language choice or document a justified region-specific constraint.","remediation":"Make the transcription language configurable by the caller, allow automatic detection without forcing a locale, or clearly document and justify any required language restriction.","code_snippet":null,"intent":null,"tags":["llm-unconfirmed"],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":null,"occurrences":[{"file":"src/subtitle.py","start_line":419,"end_line":419}]},{"id":"SDI-4","finding_id":"finding-9c43fe305733482498aaa431fdc9b11e","category":null,"pattern":null,"severity":"MEDIUM","confidence":0.88,"location":{"file":"src/utils.py","start_line":164,"end_line":186},"finding":null,"explanation":"The docstring states the returned value is 'safe to pass as a positional argv element to a subprocess,' but the implementation only sanitizes filename characters and a leading dash. It does not guarantee broader subprocess safety properties beyond this narrow context, so the documentation overclaims what the code ensures and could mislead developers about the function's security guarantees.","remediation":"Narrow the docstring to describe the exact protections implemented, such as path separator replacement, control character removal, and leading-dash neutralization. Avoid blanket claims of subprocess safety unless the function's contract and all call sites enforce those guarantees.","code_snippet":null,"intent":null,"tags":["llm-unconfirmed"],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":null,"occurrences":[{"file":"src/utils.py","start_line":164,"end_line":186}]},{"id":"SDI-4","finding_id":"finding-404ba0fa362948e99709a8e6023204fd","category":null,"pattern":null,"severity":"LOW","confidence":0.95,"location":{"file":"README.md","start_line":437,"end_line":437},"finding":null,"explanation":"The README presents contradictory statements about credential persistence: one section says credentials are not persisted by default except via manual save_to_file(), while earlier sections document automatic persistence through persist=True or BILIBILI_PERSIST. This inconsistency can mislead users into enabling disk storage of sensitive cookies without fully realizing it, increasing the chance of accidental credential exposure on shared or compromised systems.","remediation":"Make the persistence behavior consistent and explicit in all documentation. State clearly whether persistence can occur automatically when enabled, where the file is stored, and under what conditions it is created/loaded; remove or rewrite the claim that manual save_to_file() is the only persistence path.","code_snippet":null,"intent":null,"tags":[],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":null,"occurrences":[{"file":"README.md","start_line":437,"end_line":437}]},{"id":"SQP-3","finding_id":"finding-57cd96b145f3465d850fcca0888b782b","category":null,"pattern":null,"severity":"LOW","confidence":0.93,"location":{"file":"skill.json","start_line":224,"end_line":227},"finding":null,"explanation":"The manifest defines a subtitle language preference with a default of 'zh-CN'. Forcing a specific language/locale by default can conflict with language-choice policy when the skill does not explicitly offer user opt-in or explain that the default is user-configurable based on preference.","remediation":"Remove the fixed locale default, or make language selection explicit at runtime. Alternatively, document that the language is configurable and defaults to the video's native subtitle language or the user's stated preference rather than a hardcoded locale.","code_snippet":null,"intent":null,"tags":["llm-unconfirmed"],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":null,"occurrences":[{"file":"skill.json","start_line":224,"end_line":227}]},{"id":"SQP-1","finding_id":"finding-bd5061a6c953449e9a571a8dc30e0526","category":null,"pattern":null,"severity":"LOW","confidence":0.83,"location":{"file":"skill.json","start_line":416,"end_line":416},"finding":null,"explanation":"This manifest file is in scope for vague-trigger review. The activation note says the skill should activate for 'Bilibili-related operations' and not on keyword/link detection, but it does not define concrete trigger phrases, exclusion examples, or boundaries between Bilibili-related and unrelated video tasks, which can leave invocation decisions open to interpretation.","remediation":"Add explicit activation examples and non-examples, such as a concrete list of supported intents ('download a Bilibili video', 'publish to Bilibili', 'fetch Bilibili subtitles') and exclusions ('generic video download', 'YouTube playback', 'any request containing a bilibili.com link unless the user asks to operate on it').","code_snippet":null,"intent":null,"tags":["llm-unconfirmed"],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":null,"occurrences":[{"file":"skill.json","start_line":416,"end_line":416}]},{"id":"SQP-2","finding_id":"finding-4cef20b7b6654169b8aa39b5631b8412","category":null,"pattern":null,"severity":"LOW","confidence":0.85,"location":{"file":"src/subtitle.py","start_line":490,"end_line":520},"finding":null,"explanation":"The danmaku fallback stores fetched comment data to disk automatically when captions are unavailable, without clear user disclosure or opt-in. Although the data comes from the video context rather than local secrets, it still expands the data collected and persisted beyond the user's likely expectation of subtitle downloading.","remediation":"Make danmaku fallback opt-in, clearly label it as comment extraction rather than subtitle retrieval, and warn users before saving comment-derived text to disk. Provide controls to disable persistence or store results in a temporary location unless explicitly requested.","code_snippet":null,"intent":null,"tags":[],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":null,"occurrences":[{"file":"src/subtitle.py","start_line":490,"end_line":520}]},{"id":"SDI-4","finding_id":"finding-8c0672dcfc4246d79b340e97b9a3f4c8","category":null,"pattern":null,"severity":"LOW","confidence":0.81,"location":{"file":"src/subtitle.py","start_line":531,"end_line":539},"finding":null,"explanation":"The execute docstring frames actions in terms of subtitle operations such as download, list, convert, and merge, but invoking 'download' can also trigger audio transcription and danmaku retrieval through fallback logic when no CC subtitles exist. This documentation is misleading because it describes a narrower intent than the actual side effects and outputs of the action.","remediation":"Amend the execute and download documentation to state that 'download' may invoke transcription and danmaku fallback strategies, including temporary audio download and locally saved generated outputs.","code_snippet":null,"intent":null,"tags":["llm-unconfirmed"],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":null,"occurrences":[{"file":"src/subtitle.py","start_line":531,"end_line":539}]},{"id":"SQP-3","finding_id":"finding-3b199c4932df4012b6265674a6bf9c0e","category":null,"pattern":null,"severity":"LOW","confidence":0.91,"location":{"file":"src/utils.py","start_line":141,"end_line":146},"finding":null,"explanation":"The docstring and implementation of `format_number` explicitly format values using the Chinese units `万` and `亿`. This imposes a specific locale/language convention in user-facing output without offering a choice or documenting that the skill is intentionally region-specific.","remediation":"Make number formatting locale-aware or configurable, or document that the skill is specifically intended for Chinese/Bilibili audiences. If appropriate, provide an opt-in or fallback format for non-Chinese users.","code_snippet":null,"intent":null,"tags":["llm-unconfirmed"],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":null,"occurrences":[{"file":"src/utils.py","start_line":141,"end_line":146}]}],"suppressed_count":0,"suppressed":[],"metadata":{"has_executable_scripts":true,"skillspector_version":"2.11.2","llm_requested":true,"llm_available":true,"meta_analysis_applied":true,"inference_usage":[{"node":"mcp_tool_poisoning","request_kind":"structured_output","provider":"openai","model":"gpt-5.4-2026-03-05","model_source":"provider_response","usage_source":"provider_response","prompt_tokens":1551,"completion_tokens":246,"cached_tokens":0,"reasoning_tokens":0,"total_tokens":1797},{"node":"mcp_tool_poisoning","request_kind":"structured_output","provider":"openai","model":"gpt-5.4-2026-03-05","model_source":"provider_response","usage_source":"provider_response","prompt_tokens":1371,"completion_tokens":291,"cached_tokens":0,"reasoning_tokens":0,"total_tokens":1662},{"node":"mcp_tool_poisoning","request_kind":"structured_output","provider":"openai","model":"gpt-5.4-2026-03-05","model_source":"provider_response","usage_source":"provider_response","prompt_tokens":477,"completion_tokens":176,"cached_tokens":0,"reasoning_tokens":0,"total_tokens":653},{"node":"mcp_tool_poisoning","request_kind":"structured_output","provider":"openai","model":"gpt-5.4-2026-03-05","model_so